r the fall of the Afsharids, seized Isfahan in 1750 and with Karim Khan Zand installed the young…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mirza-karkiya"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mirza Karkiya</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mirza Karkiya was a ruler of the Karkiya dynasty of Zaydi sayyids in eastern Gilan, on Iran's Caspian coast, with his seat at Lahijan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mohammed-khan"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mohammed Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mohammed Khan was the founder of Rohilla power in Rohilkhand, the region east of the upper Ganges.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mohsen-al-ahmar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-mohsen-al-ahmar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mohsen al-Ahmar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mohsen al-Ahmar is a Yemeni general, for decades one of the most powerful military commanders under President Ali Abdullah Saleh, from the same Sanhan tribe.</span></a></li></ul>
